            <ArticleTitle>Double balloon catheter for concomitant augmentation of abdominal organ perfusion during intraaortic balloon counterpulsation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>162-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A newly devised double balloon catheter to augment abdominal organ perfusion concomitant with original cardiac assist during intraaortic balloon counterpulsation provided satisfactory hemodynamics and urinary output around cardiac surgical procedures in 2 patients with coronary artery disease. Some optional advantages in clinical application and problems arising in the catheter design which need to be investigated are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
